# Monorepo root .gitignore -- app/mobile/.gitignore covers the Flutter
# app's own build artifacts (root-anchored patterns, kept scoped to where
# Flutter actually lives now). This file covers app/web (Next.js),
# app/api (Rust), and repo-wide tooling/OS/editor junk.

# Node / pnpm (app/web, packages/shared)
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.next/
out/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Rust (app/api) -- Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: app/api is a
# binary crate (a deployed service), not a library, so the lockfile is
# committed for reproducible builds, same convention as pnpm-lock.yaml.
target/

# Env / secrets -- never committed, per CLAUDE.md's key-only secret-handling rule
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Docker
*.pid

# Editors / OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.iml
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Logs
*.log

# Next.js build output.
#
# This was `_next/` until 16 Sep 2026, filed under "Logs", which it is not.
# The only `_next` directory in this repo is `/_next/` at the root -- the
# project's BACKLOG, the same `_next/` convention every project on the drive
# uses. So that rule ignored no build output whatsoever and instead hid 20
# live backlog rows from git. Because this repo is nested inside the _kit
# checkout (which cannot track another repo's contents), those rows existed
# in exactly one place: one disk, no remote, no backup.
#
# Next.js actually emits `.next/` while developing and `out/` on export --
# and `out/_next/` is covered by the `out/` rule, so nothing is lost.
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
